<title>JAPAN: Two Osaka credit associations say to merge in Nov.</title>
<headline>Two Osaka credit associations say to merge in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>OSAKA, Japan 1996-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two Osaka-based credit associations, known as &quot;shinkin&quot; banks, said on Thursday they will merge in November.</p>
<p>The two associations -- Hakko Shinkin Bank and Osaka Sangyo Shinyo Kinko -- said they will hold a joint news conference at Thursday noon (0300 GMT) to announce details of the merger.  </p>
<p>This would be the third such credit association merger in Osaka announced so far this year. Credit associations lend money mainly to members, but take deposits widely. Most borrowers are small and medium-sized businesses.</p>
</text>
